WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.159
Let's get into audience questions for the
week.

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:05.850
First one is, hey, David, is being against
immigration necessarily racist?

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.080
Couldn't you simply be against immigration,
but not for racist or xenophobic reasons?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.080
Yeah.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.740
I mean, listen, this is I prefer to deal in
reality rather than than in hypotheticals.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:21.110
Of course, it's possible that you might be
someone who does not care about race or ethnicity.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:26.460
You're against immigration to the United States
from any country for any reason whatsoever.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.690
Doesn't matter if it's a country of predominantly
white or brown people or if it's a predominantly

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.200
rich or poor country.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.200
Sure.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.320
That that exists.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:44.160
The reality is that in in a vast swaths of
situations, the economic arguments that you

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:51.000
often hear made against immigration really
only end up applying to or people are only

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.430
thinking of those from countries where the
immigrants are more brown or black than they

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.200
are white.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.760
And we see this in a number of different ways,
which we'll talk about.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.950
You can for sure.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:12.110
I mean, listen, first of all, there are studies
that show that racism and anti-immigrant sentiment

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.610
are highly correlated.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:20.270
Now, you could be racist and against immigration
for other reasons that are not related to

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.720
race or ethnicity.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.220
Sure, that that's quite possible.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:30.479
But decades of data show us that preconceived
prejudicial notions about race and race and

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:36.150
ethnicity tend to correlate with anti-immigrant
sentiment.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:41.670
Now, there are many economic questions about
immigration that can be made.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:48.070
We've analyzed many of them, like, for example,
immigrants are taking the jobs of Americans.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.500
Immigrants reduce wages.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.580
Immigrants are leeching off of the system.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.000
And every single one of these has an answer.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.690
And it's typically not what the anti-immigration
crowd says.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.990
One of the things I think is useful when you're
dealing with

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.630
someone who
claims to be just against immigration, period,

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:16.930
is to talk about a situation in which the
immigrants are typically whites from so-called

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:22.810
Western nations and gauge the reaction to
that situation and then talk about immigrants

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.910
from countries where people tend to be brown
or black.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:31.790
Or at least the belief is when you talk about
immigrants from Mexico or Haiti, the people

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:32.790
aren't white.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:33.900
And see if you get the same reaction.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.310
I mean, it's you know, we can study these
things scientifically and empirically and

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.310
it's been done.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:45.070
But when when you have such a situation, if
it's someone, you know, gauge their reaction,

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.390
talk about immigrants from Norway and Sweden
and then talk about immigrants from from Haiti

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.420
or Mexico or whatever, whatever the case may
be.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.030
Now, they may say, well, I have a different
opinion about immigrants from Sweden versus

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.120
immigrants from Haiti, but it's not because
of race.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.800
It's because it's about skill.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:10.129
And I believe that for no racially motivated
reason, the people coming from Sweden are

00:03:10.129 --> 00:03:14.730
higher skilled than the person than the people
coming from Haiti.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:22.930
The reality is that there's plenty of highly
skilled computer programmers, engineers, people

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:30.470
in the medical field, accountants coming from
Africa, some of the top engineering and programing

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:33.800
people that I know in the United States are
from Argentina now.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.440
There's an availability bias for sure, me
being from Argentina.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.300
I just know more Argentineans also.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.450
Argentina's mostly white, but a lot of racists
don't realize that they don't know the difference

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:49.080
between Argentina and Mexico and, you know,
Costa Rica or whatever the case may be.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.440
But this is you know, I'm reminded of the
situation with the Israeli BDS movement where

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:58.019
in principle, just saying for political reasons,
Israel should be boycotted.

00:03:58.019 --> 00:03:59.700
That's not anti-Semitic.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:06.860
But the BDS movement is a haven for and provides
cover for many anti-Semitic whose reasons

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:11.920
stated for boycotting Israel could apply to
10 other countries which they either aren't

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.349
even aware of or are aware of, but certainly
aren't interested or advocating in boycotting.

00:04:16.349 --> 00:04:18.560
So, yes, you can be.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.479
I mean, if you're just trying to get me to
say

00:04:21.479 --> 00:04:23.449
you can
be against immigration and not be a racist.

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:24.639
Of course.

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:25.639
Of course.

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:31.419
Now that we've gotten back beyond the hypothetical,
let's actually deal with the typical reasons

00:04:31.419 --> 00:04:36.059
that are given for being against immigration
and see if they're applied equally regardless

00:04:36.059 --> 00:04:37.400
of of race or ethnicity.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:05:36.849
And you very quickly see how it is a cover
for lots of racists 

00:05:36.849 --> 00:05:48.530
and xenophobes,

